abstract: |
  Pantheon Trades is a structured-deliberation trading system for
  prediction markets. An eleven-agent AI council debates every
  candidate trade across four rounds (opening, challenge, synthesis,
  vote) using role-divergent prompts. Each refusal is anchored as
  a Proof of Restraint witness on Circle's Arc Testnet so the
  discipline of NOT trading becomes auditable.

  Empirically: on a 200-market resolved Manifold sample, council
  aggregation lowers Brier score from 0.260 (single-shot Gemini)
  to 0.149, closing approximately 80% of the gap to the
  free-play-money human-consensus baseline at 0.126.

  The system implements Murphy (1973) Brier-score decomposition,
  beta calibration (Kull et al. 2017), per-category Platt scaling,
  Brier-weighted council aggregation, and conformal Kelly sizing
  against a held-out prediction-interval lower bound.

